Exception: kernel_ridge_fit_host: the ridged kernel matrix K + alpha I is NOT positive definite (info=259, the leading minor of order 259 failed). kernel=sigmoid, n_samples=515. cuML catches this and silently returns a LEAST-SQUARES solution instead (kernel_ridge.py:26-44, behind a warnings.warn); this lane refuses, because a fit that returns a different estimator than the one it was asked for is a wrong answer with no error. THE CLOSURE IS alpha: raise it. A float32 kernel matrix needs a larger ridge than cuML's float64 one at the same data (DEVIATION 1661). To close it properly, implementation an SVD-based least-squares arm -- there is one at solver/checks/lstsq.mojo -- and gate BOTH sides of the branch; kernel_methods/NOT_IMPLEMENTED.tsv carries the row
